        "source": "import triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n@triton.jit\ndef softmax_stats(X, S, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    offs = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    idx = row * N + offs\n    mask = offs < N\n    x = tl.load(X + idx, mask, other=-float('inf'))\n    mx = tl.max(x, 0)\n    exps = tl.exp(x - mx)\n    denom = tl.sum(exps, 0)\n    tl.store(S + row * 2, mx)\n    tl.store(S + row * 2 + 1, denom)\n\n@triton.jit\ndef softmax_apply(X, S, Y, TOTAL: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    i = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    mask = i < TOTAL\n    row = i // N\n    x = tl.load(X + i, mask, other=0)\n    mx = tl.load(S + row * 2, mask, other=0)\n    denom = tl.load(S + row * 2 + 1, mask, other=1)\n    y = tl.exp(x - mx) / denom\n    tl.store(Y + i, y, mask)\n",
        "rationale": "Reverted to original num_warps=4 and num_stages=1 to ensure numerical stability and correctness, since increased warp count and stages caused NaN errors. Adjusted softmax_apply grid from 1570 to 1571 to fully cover the input elements. This preserves stable numerics and masking while ensuring all input elements are processed correctly, balancing occupancy and correctness."
